<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 1088 0 R
/T (The rectifier serves as the interface between the AC supply system and the DC traction motor. Due to the nonlinear switching action of the diodes, the rectifier draws a non- sinusoidal current from the AC source, resulting in harmonic distortion in the supply current waveform. These harmonics are the primary source of power quality issues investigated in this project. )
/E (The rectifier serves as the interface between the AC supply system and the DC traction motor. Due to the nonlinear switching action of the diodes, the rectifier draws a non- sinusoidal current from the AC source, resulting in harmonic distortion in the supply current waveform. These harmonics are the primary source of power quality issues investigated in this project. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1470 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 1088 0 R
/T (To improve the quality of the DC output, a series smoothing choke is connected at the rectifier output. The smoothing choke reduces current ripple supplied to the PMDC motor and promotes continuous current operation. Under these operating conditions, lower-order harmonics such as the 3rd, 5th, and 7th harmonics become dominant components ofthe source current spectrum, which were subsequently analyzed using FFT techniquesand mitigated using passive harmonic filters.  3.5 DC Motor)
/E (To improve the quality of the DC output, a series smoothing choke is connected at the rectifier output. The smoothing choke reduces current ripple supplied to the PMDC motor and promotes continuous current operation. Under these operating conditions, lower-order harmonics such as the 3rd, 5th, and 7th harmonics become dominant components ofthe source current spectrum, which were subsequently analyzed using FFT techniquesand mitigated using passive harmonic filters.  3.5 DC Motor)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
