/P 1088 0 R
/T (The mechanical traction load is represented by the Maxon RE6538898970 permanent magnet DC motor. This motor is widely used in laboratory-scale traction emulation rigs because its catalogue parameters \(rated voltage, no-load speed, stall torque, armature inductance and resistance\) are readily available and accurately documented by the manufacturer. The motor specifications used in the simulation are summarised in Table 3.1. )
/E (The mechanical traction load is represented by the Maxon RE6538898970 permanent magnet DC motor. This motor is widely used in laboratory-scale traction emulation rigs because its catalogue parameters \(rated voltage, no-load speed, stall torque, armature inductance and resistance\) are readily available and accurately documented by the manufacturer. The motor specifications used in the simulation are summarised in Table 3.1. )
