/T (The waveform is visibly far closer to a sinusoid than the unfiltered case in Fig. 4.1. The sharp pulses have been smoothed out and the current now flows continuously throughout each half-cycle. Small ripples and a mild double-hump near the peak remain, due to residual higher-order harmonics that are not directly targeted by the 3rd, 5th and 7th filters. The corresponding FFT spectrum is shown in Fig. 5.3. )
/E (The waveform is visibly far closer to a sinusoid than the unfiltered case in Fig. 4.1. The sharp pulses have been smoothed out and the current now flows continuously throughout each half-cycle. Small ripples and a mild double-hump near the peak remain, due to residual higher-order harmonics that are not directly targeted by the 3rd, 5th and 7th filters. The corresponding FFT spectrum is shown in Fig. 5.3. )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [3]
>>
