/Title (Thisprojectpresentsthemodellingandanalysisofasingle-phase AC electric tractionpowersupplysystemusingMATLAB/Simulink,withafocus on improving source-sidepowerqualitythroughpassiveharmonicfilters.Modernrailway traction networksrelyheavilyonpowerelectronicconvertersandrectifier-fed motor drives. Whiletheseconvertersenablecontrolled,efficientpropulsion,theybehave as non- linearloadsandinjectsignificantharmoniccurrentsintothesupply network. The injectedharmonicsdistortthesourcecurrentwaveform,degradethedisplacement and distortioncomponentsofthepowerfactor,increasecopperandironlosses in the feeder transformer,andmayinterferewithneighborsignallingandcommunication circuits.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 6090 0 R
/Next 6096 0 R
>>
endobj
6093 0 obj
<<
/Title (Tomitigatetheseeffects,threeshunt-connectedsingle-tunedpassive harmonic filtersaredesignedforthe3rd,5thand7thharmonicfrequenciesand integrated on the ACsideoftherectifier.Withthefiltersinservice,theTHDofthesupply current is reducedtoapproximately7.65%,thepowerfactorisimprovedto0.82, and the AC currentwaveformbecomessubstantiallyclosertoacleansinusoid.The comparative resultsconfirmthatsimple,well-tunedpassivefiltersareacost-effective and reliable meansofimprovingthepowerqualityofsingle-phaseACtractionsystems and meeting harmoniccompliancelimitsrecommended byIEEE 519andIEC 61000-2-4.)
