/Title (The unfiltered Simulink model described in Chapter 3 is simulated for a duration sufficient to reach steady state. The simulation is then continued for several additional fundamental cycles to enable a clean FFT analysis. The AC supply current waveform obtained in the steady state is shown in Fig. 4.1. The waveform is markedly different from a pure sinusoid: it exhibits sharp, narrow peaks of opposite polarity that coincide with the conduction intervals of the bridge rectifier, separated by intervals of essentially zero current. This pulse-like shape is characteristic of a single-phase diode-bridge rectifier feeding a strongly inductive DC load.)
